        "self_reported": {
          "assumptions": [
            "Windows CPython 3.12's finalizer treats a daemon thread blocked in os.read on fd 0 like Linux 3.13's does (no lock to take, process exit ends the thread); validation.sh's interop check verifies this on the laptop and fails loudly if it hangs or errors"
          ],
          "judgment_calls": [
            "Mechanism: os.read on the raw stdin fd, chosen over closing stdin from the shim (the shim cannot know the recording finished before the child exits), joining with a timeout (the read never returns), and os._exit (skips logging shutdown and hides future finalizer problems)",
            "Any bytes on stdin now count as a stop, where before a full line did; the shim always sends one 'stop\\n' write and a console read returns on Enter, so no real input behaves differently",
            "No probe: confirmation on the laptop moved into validation.sh's interop check, which skips with a reason where python.exe is unreachable",
            "The wasapi capture child has the same buffered-stdin pattern on its error exits; left alone (audio is out of scope) and proposed in notes.md"
          ],
